<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolsa Família</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2003">2003</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bolsa Família is a Brazilian social programme that pays monthly cash transfers to poor families on condition that their children attend school and are vaccinated. Created in 2003 under President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luiz-inacio-lula-da-silva">Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva</a> by merging earlier schemes, it reached about a quarter of the population and is credited with sharply reducing extreme poverty. Renamed Auxílio Brasil under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jair-bolsonaro">Jair Bolsonaro</a>, it was restored under its old name in 2023.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bolsa-familia.jpg" alt="Bolsa Família" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Secretaria de Comunicação Social / Governo Federal do Brasil · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_Bolsa_Fam%C3%ADlia_2023.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
